== Usage ==
:''To see how this spell is used with the contraption, See: [[Floatglow Lamp]]''
Floatglow Lamp is a spell in the ''Basics of Spellcasting Primer'', specifically the Wall-Anchored version. It is one of the spells [[Euini]] prepares in advance prior to retaking the [[Sincerity of the Shield|second test]].{{Ref|a|12}}

[[Coco]] practices this seal during her lessons with [[Qifrey]].{{Ref|a|11}}

When [[Agott]], [[Tetia]], and Coco are brainstorming ways to save Euini, The Floatglow Lamp seal is proposed as a spell with the potential to help them reach their goal.{{Ref|m|28|10}}

== Trivia ==
* Given that the effect for Floatglow Lamp (Ch. 28) has never been shown and the seal for the Wall-Anchored Floatglow Lamp (Vol. 12 Extra Page) has been used for contraptions that are not exclusively anchored to the wall, it is possible that the original Floatglow Lamp (Ch. 28) has been retconned, much like the original Pyreball seal.{{Cite}}
** Pyreball also used Signs of Level Planes before being changed to Signs of Levitation.{{Cite}}
** Floatglow Lamps that are used like lanterns have not had their casting seals shown. It’s possible that these lantern variants are the ones using the Chapter 28 casting seal, and the Signs of Level Planes are functioning to float the lamp’s top, bottom ''and'' the ball of light.{{Cite}}
** There are still Floatglow Lamps that are technically anchored to the wall and have a floating tray.{{Ref|m|14|25-26}}
